60,3,1,talk,Servas,,The candidates are here. We must choose who truly has the hands and the time to deliver.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Servas, I agree. We must match the science to the available hands and the stable infrastructure.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Servas, I agree. We must pick the project that fits the glasshouse crew and avoids the broken spectroscopy suite.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @Kenji, avoiding the broken suite is smart. But we must also avoid the breeding colonies that overrun schedules.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, agreed. But I need to know which of these four actually delivered results in the past, not just which avoids current bottlenecks.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, the closeout files show catalogue-style work endures, while mechanism-focused projects often stall. Which candidate fits that enduring pattern?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Toshio, I agree. The Microbiome Atlas fits that enduring catalogue pattern, and the free compute helps with the sequence analysis.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, the Atlas relies on field sites. My records show three lost a season to flooding. Is that risk worth the catalogue prize?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, field loss is a setback, not a stop. The Atlas can still publish from the two stable sites.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, partial delivery is not delivery. The closeout files show mechanism-focused work often ends unresolved. I need certainty, not hope.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, certainty is a luxury. The Atlas delivers data now, while the others risk stalling. I vote for the Atlas.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I agree. The Atlas fits the stable infrastructure and the enduring catalogue pattern. I vote for the Atlas.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Toshio, the field risk is real, but the greenhouse is full. The Atlas is the only one that fits the available space. I vote for the Atlas.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the Atlas is the only one that avoids the breeding overruns and the broken spectroscopy. I vote for the Atlas.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, the closeout files confirm catalogue work endures. The Atlas is the only candidate with a proven track record of delivery. I vote for the Atlas.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,The vote is unanimous. The Microbiome Atlas is selected. We have chosen the path of reliable delivery over uncertain promise.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I am glad we found common ground. The Atlas balances the science with the reality of our current resources.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Servas, I’m happy we picked the one that actually fits our current capacity. Good call, everyone.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @Servas, a unanimous vote is rare. I hope the Atlas delivers as reliably as the closeout files suggest.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the files do not lie. The Atlas is the only choice that respects the evidence.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
